<code>assert index >= 0 && index <= \old(this.size()) && role != null => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i+1)) == null) || this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i+1)));</code>

However, there seems to be a slight mistake in the logic of the assertion. The correct assertion should compare the elements correctly without the need for both elements to be null. Here's the corrected version:

<code>assert index >= 0 && index <= \old(this.size()) && role != null => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i+1)));</code>

But since the element at the insertion point `index` will be replaced by `role`, the correct comparison should start from `index + 1`. Therefore, the final correct assertion is:

<code>assert index >= 0 && index <= \old(this.size()) && role != null => \forall int i; index < i && i < \old(this.size()); this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i-1)));</code>
